      "content": "Taking 1000mg of magnesium daily is likely too high, especially since those large doses are frequently found in over-the-counter laxatives that are generally not suitable for regular therapeutic use. Because you have a history of kidney issues, you must consult your doctor before starting any magnesium supplements, as impaired kidney function prevents the body from properly excreting excess magnesium, which can be dangerous. Magnesium levels can build up to toxic levels quickly in individuals with compromised kidneys, leading to severe health complications.",
